}{}\begin{eqnarray*}{H}^{(l+1)}=\sigma ({\widetilde {D}}^{- \frac{1}{2} }\widetilde {A}{\widetilde {D}}^{- \frac{1}{2} }{H}^{ \left( l \right) }{W}^{ \left( l \right) })\end{eqnarray*}\end{document}Hl+1=σD ˜−12A ˜D ˜−12HlWl
knowing that H(0
) = X, W(l) represents a layer-specific trainable weight matrix, σ(.) is an activation function, H(l) ∈ ℝn×d is the activation matrix in the lth layer.

