where MLP (⋅) is a multi-layer perceptron, and s is a learnable scaling factor. In practice, s is set to be a learnable scalar with an initialized value of 1.

To define a convolution in a hypergraph, Bai, Zhang & Torr (2021) assumed that more propagation functions should be applied on the nodes linked by a common hyperedge, and the hyperedges with larger weights deserve more confidence in such a propagation. The proposed the hypergraph convolution is demonstrated as: (12)\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
